Geckos are usually small to medium-sized with slender bodies;
Their heads have visible eyes with excellent night vision;
They have long tails that can be shed as a defense mechanism;
Geckos have strong, adhereable toes with specialized lamellae for climbing;
Their feet allow them to climb smooth and vertical surfaces;
Most geckos can vocalize, producing various sounds;
They have soft, granular skin that can be smooth or granulated;
Many geckos have the ability to glide through the air, using their extensive skin flaps;
Geckos generally have excellent hearing, with ears located behind their eyes;
Many possess the ability to detach their tails to distract predators;
Their diet consists of insects, including crickets, mealworms, and cockroaches;
Geckos have a vertical pupils, which are adapted for nocturnal hunting;
They often have the ability to eyelid-opening, which helps keep their eyes clean and free from dust;
Some geckos have the capability to regenerate lost tails over time.
